1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
With AI, anyone can build little web apps

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,000
— just for themselves.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,300
But they're scattered all over your Mac.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:11,900
Some pages just open and work.

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,000
Others only load through a local server.

6
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,000
What if they all had one home?

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,600
Meet LocalServe.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,500
It turns any folder into a local site — no terminal, no cloud.

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Pick the folder, choose a port…

10
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,500
…and hit start. That's it.

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,500
That blank page from before? Now it just works.

12
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Need more? Here are a few power features.

13
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,300
When your local site calls a remote server directly,

14
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,800
it usually gets blocked by CORS.

15
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:47,000
Add a proxy rule in LocalServe, and it goes through.

16
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,800
You can give each site a memorable domain name.

17
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:52,500
LocalServe manages hosts for you.

18
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:57,000
You can also open your sites on any device by scanning the QR code,

19
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,400
as long as it's on the same Wi-Fi.

20
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,400
Same goes for file sharing.

21
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,800
Pick. Scan. Done. No cables, no cloud.

22
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,700
Try it free for seven days — no account needed.

23
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,300
Then buy once, and it's yours forever.

24
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:14,000
LocalServe. All your little apps, one home.
